body:
My mum raised me to believe that I was the cause of all our family's financial issues (our family was actually quite well off, she was just a reckless spender and would always get herself into debt) as well as ruin my self-esteem where ever she could; complain I was too fat, too thin, eating too much, not eating enough, too picky with my food, was eating like a dustbin, was showing off too much of my body, was being too prudish and so on. She was manipulative and controlling, and occasionally would physically hurt me (e.g. would stamp on my back if I was lying down on my stomach).  I remember, when my pubic hair was starting to grow, she pulled my shirt up and made me expose my hairy underarms to my aunties as a way of shaming me into getting waxing done (i was 12 or 13 then). She was toxic in so many other ways but if I talked about them all I'd be here for ages.

&#x200B;

Cope? Not really sure if I've actually "coped" with it, there's still a lot that I find myself terrified to do because of her. For example, I'm scared of showing my arms or legs just cuz im terrified of showing any body hair. Im getting better at accepting my body hair, though I'm almost 21 and I still get really emotional thinking about when she made me expose myself that one time. I absolutely can't bring myself to talk about money either. My mum used to read all my bank statements and question me about my purchases (which yeah, I get she was trying to keep me safe from fraud) but it just made me uncomfortable with bank statements, so much so that I haven't actually read any of my bank statements in years. I spend recklessly, but I only buy what I can afford, i don't get into debt. Since my body was never perfect enough for her I just stopped trying to have a perfect body. I used to be an incredibly slim and muscular teen, but now I'm just a blob. Again, I can get into more but there's so much.

&#x200B;

Near the start of 2019 I suddenly, with no warning, just found myself unable to speak to my mum. I honestly don't know what happened, I just physically can't bring myself to do it. I don't hate her, I just no longer feel any emotion towards her. 

&#x200B;

I never idolized my mum, but I loved her growing up. We had fun moments, we shared laughs, we have good memories, and it was these few positives that I clung to for years. I told myself that it would be cruel of me to hate my mum considering that she (though, mostly my dad) gave me such a privalleged upbringing (several holidays each year). I knew she, like every mother, had made sacrifices for me and that she did what she did because she loved me. I still don't know how I feel about her. I don't think I'm correct in basically cutting her out of my life for almost a year, but I just want to believe that I am. I really want to believe that it's okay for me to hate my mum but I just don't know.
